---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/cascadia-systems-lab/cascadia-lab.github.io';
---

<Layout
  title="Infrastructure"
  description="Field instruments and self-hosted processing infrastructure at Cascadia Mobile Research"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
        <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Infrastructure</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary">
          Two halves of one pipeline: instruments that collect data in the field, and the
          self-hosted compute that turns it into deliverables.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Field Instruments -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Field Instruments</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">Sub-250g UAS Platform</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A lightweight quadcopter platform for aerial imagery, mapping capture, and inspection
            work. Staying under 250 grams is a deliberate operational choice: lower risk profile,
            simpler compliance, and surprisingly capable imaging for photogrammetry.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">Handheld 3D LiDAR Scanner</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A portable LiDAR unit with SLAM-based processing for scanning structures, sites, and
            interiors — the spaces aerial capture can't reach. Output is registered point clouds
            ready for modeling and measurement.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">Capture Planning &amp; Ground Truth</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Repeatable flight and scan planning so the same site can be captured consistently over
            time, plus ground-reference workflows for checking reconstruction accuracy against
            reality.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card border-dashed">
          <div class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-secondary">In Development</h3>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-accent-purple/20 px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-accent-purple">
              Roadmap
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A custom-built freestyle-class UAV for specialized capture work, and sensor payloads
            for geophysical survey — documented in the lab notes as they progress.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Processing Backend -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Processing Backend</h2>
      <div class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-4xl">
        <p class="text-center text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          Everything captured in the field is processed on infrastructure the lab owns and
          operates. No third-party cloud processing, no black boxes — a pipeline we can measure,
          tune, and explain.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-blue">GPU Workstation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A dedicated modern-GPU workstation runs the heavy reconstruction work: photogrammetry,
            point cloud processing, and machine learning workloads including self-hosted model
            inference.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-cyan">Virtualization Cluster</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            A multi-node Proxmox cluster hosts the lab's services and processing pipelines —
            including the LiDAR SLAM environment — with workloads isolated in VMs and containers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-green">Tiered Storage</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            NVMe for active reconstruction workloads, high-capacity disk arrays for datasets,
            deliverable archives, and project history. Field data is redundantly stored from the
            day it's captured.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold text-accent-purple">Monitoring &amp; Operations</h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Observability across the stack — utilization, job progress, and system health — so
            processing time and cost per project are measured facts, not guesses.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Infrastructure as Research -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">The Backend Is Also a Research Subject</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Running our own processing stack raises questions worth answering in public: what does
            self-hosted photogrammetry cost against cloud services? How should storage and compute
            be sized for reconstruction workloads? Where are the real bottlenecks? We benchmark our
            own infrastructure and publish the results in the
            <a href="/research" class="link">lab notes</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Documentation Links -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">Specifications &amp; Docs</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-text-secondary">
          A complete hardware inventory with specifications and performance baselines is being
          built out in the repository, alongside configuration docs and operational runbooks.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a
            href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/hardware/INVENTORY.md`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="btn btn-primary"
          >
            Hardware Inventory
          </a>
          <a href="/documentation" class="btn btn-secondary">
            All Documentation
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
